# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIDENTIALITY BOUNDARY — do not relax any rule in this block.
# Everything here is CLINICAL material: her documents, session recordings,
# session transcripts and generated guidance. It stays on the private box.
#
# Paths are anchored with a leading slash so they match only at the repo root.
# An unanchored rule like "transcripts/" also silently matches
# library/transcripts/, which is public-source material, not clinical.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
library/sources/private/
/sessions/
/transcripts/
/audio/
/guidance/
*.docx
*.doc
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.mp4
*.srt
couples.yaml
couple-map*
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Third-party text: fetched pages and generated podcast transcripts are copies of other people's
# work. They are rebuilt locally from sources.yaml (fetch + scripts/transcribe_feed.py) and never
# published. The registry keeps the citation; the text stays on the machine that fetched it.
library/raw/
library/transcripts/

# derived artefacts: large, binary, and rebuilt from library/raw + sources.yaml
library/index/
library/_podcast_work/

# secrets
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
credentials*.json
service-account*.json
rclone.conf

# models (large, re-downloadable)
models/
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin

# python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# os / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
